1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,000
Text Justification — LeetCode 68

2
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:06,200
Problem: pack words into lines of exactly maxWidth characters, both edges flush.

3
00:00:06,200 --> 00:00:10,000
With maxWidth 16, these seven words become three fully-justified lines.

4
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:13,600
Three rules do it all.

5
00:00:13,600 --> 00:00:18,000
One: greedily pack as many words as fit. Two: spread the leftover spaces evenly.

6
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:22,500
When they don't divide evenly, the left-hand gaps take the extras. Three: the last line is left-justified.

7
00:00:22,500 --> 00:00:27,000
Line one packs This, is, an — that's 10 with single spaces; adding example would be 18, too big.

8
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:31,500
Slack is 16 minus 8 letters = 8 spaces, over 2 gaps = 4 and 4. Even.

9
00:00:31,500 --> 00:00:36,500
Line two packs example, of, text. Slack 3 over 2 gaps = 2 then 1 — the left gap gets the extra.

10
00:00:36,500 --> 00:00:41,000
Line three is just justification — the last line, so single spaces and pad the right.

11
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:45,000
Every line lands on exactly 16 characters, fully justified.

12
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:49,500
Time O(N) over the total characters, O(1) extra space.

13
00:00:49,500 --> 00:00:54,000
That completes the Array and String section. AxioByte — follow for all 150.
